---
import Component from "../../../src/components/donate/GivingSoonNote.astro";
import "../../../src/styles/tokens.css";

// Isolation page for the note on a DARK band — the tone the campaign hero, the
// network rail and the closing ask use.
//
// It is a separate page rather than a `?s=` state because this is a static
// build: query params are empty at build time, so one page would capture the
// same default frame for both tones.
//
// This frame is the one that matters for legibility. The note inherited its
// colour in the first draft, which produced near-black text on this near-black
// ground — present in the DOM, unreadable on the page. `onDark` is the band
// telling the note which way to go, and this capture is what proves it did.
//
// The link is shown with its own label here: on the homepage band the note
// points at /donate ("Read about the Momentum Fund") rather than at the
// volunteer page, because a reader there has not yet been told what the fund is.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Isolated: GivingSoonNote-OnDark</title>
  </head>
  <body style="margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: #0b0b0f;">
    <div id="codeyam-capture" style="padding: var(--space-lg); width: 100%; max-width: 420px;">
      <Component onDark linkHref="/donate" linkLabel="Read about the Momentum Fund" />
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
